# Reliv PWA Backend - Environment Variables

## Required Variables

### AI API Keys
```
# Google Gemini API Key
# Get from: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...

# Groq API Key (Optional - for faster inference)
# Get from: https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
```

### Web Push (VAPID Keys)
```
# Generate once with: npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# Then set as env vars (survives restarts & redeploys)
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=B...
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=...
```

### Server Config
```
PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=production
```

## Deployment Instructions

### Render.com (Recommended Free Tier)
1. Connect GitHub repo
2. Create new Web Service
3. Select `backend/` root directory
4. Runtime: Node
5. Build: `npm install`
6. Start: `npm start`
7. Under Environment, add all variables from above

### Local Development
1. Copy .env.example to .env
2. Fill in your API keys
3. Run: `npm run dev`

## Important Security Notes

⚠️ **NEVER** commit actual .env files to version control
⚠️ **NEVER** expose API keys in frontend code
⚠️ **ALWAYS** use environment variables on production servers

The backend proxies all AI requests so keys remain protected from browser extraction.
